* text=auto
*.c text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
# .sh was missing from this list, and unlike the rest it is not cosmetic: a
# script checked out CRLF on Windows and copied to Linux does not run at all.
# The kernel reads the shebang literally, so `#!/usr/bin/env bash` + CR asks
# for an interpreter named "bash\r", and `set -euo pipefail` + CR fails as
#     tools/build.sh: line 30: set: pipefail: invalid option name
# which points at the option rather than the line ending. Found building the
# Steam Deck bundle: every script in the exported release tree was inert.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf
